  "body": "The latest work on the JS spec seems to say things like \"Let _completion_ be [Completion Record](https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-completion-record-specification-type) { [[Type]]: ..., [[Value]]: ..., [[Target]]: ... }.\"\r\n\r\nIt looks like we sometimes use `Completion {` with no link (should be `Completion Record {` with a link) and `Property Descriptor{` with a link (should have a space before `{`).\r\n\r\nFor \"untyped\" records, we mostly don't have any prefix. Sometimes we have `Record {` linked, sometimes we have `Record {` unlinked, most times we just use `{`. Some of these these are just omitting `Property Descriptor {`, which we should fix. But I don't think we should necessarily add `Record {` in front of all of them, even though the JS spec does. It's verbose and many of these could probably be converted to Infra maps anyway. (https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8363) I'm inclined to leave most of them as-is, or maybe just remove the `Record ` prefix.",
